==============================================================================
A. Per-coordinate overlap-tilt calculus on Bernoulli products
==============================================================================
Coupling of Bern(p) with itself, odds ratio rho (rho>1 = overlap-
biased).  Union marginal m(rho) = 1 - z_rho(1-p,1-p); product
obstructs the tilt iff h(m) < h(p) for ALL rho, i.e. never once
rho can exceed rho*(p) = p(3p-1)/(1-2p)^2.

z_rho validated: max odds-ratio round-trip rel. error = 5.39e-13
rho*(p) closed form:  max |z_rho*(x,x)-(1-x)| = 1.08e-14
p*(rho) closed form:  max inversion error      = 3.20e-14
continuity: p*(1) = 0.381966 = psi;  p*(1e6) = 0.499750 -> 1/2

     rho    p*(rho)   (products with p < p* never obstruct tilt rho)
  1.0000   0.381966
  1.0100   0.382214
  1.0303   0.382712
  1.1000   0.384361
  1.2500   0.387628
  1.5000   0.392375
  2.0000   0.400000
  3.0000   0.410803
  5.0000   0.424042
 10.0000   0.440498
100.0000   0.477299

Odds ratio needed to clear Liu's record 0.38271: rho*(0.38271) = 1.030222
(the tilt analogue of 002's c_needed = 0.007: a 3% odds-ratio
 tilt already moves the PRODUCT ceiling past the record --
 products are cheap; the mixture/slice adversaries decide.)

Adaptive tilt, per-coordinate: max_m h(m) - h(p) = 1 - h(p) > 0
for all p in (psi, 1/2); min over grid = 0.000000 (at p->1/2).
==> the Bernoulli-product obstruction of the adaptive overlap-
    tilt class sits at exactly 1/2 (vs psi for iid, c=0..1 KL).
  [checkpoint: ../attempts/union-closed/data/003_partA.json]

==============================================================================
B. Pure Chase-Lovett slice under the pure overlap tilt (exact)
==============================================================================
mu = Unif(slice w0 = round(p n)).  This family kills the iid
functional for p > psi (h(2p-p^2) < h(p)) and has D = inf, so 002
could only reach it via smoothing.  The tilt coupling reaches it
directly.  Gain(lam) = H_pi(U) - log2 C(n,w0):

n=  1000 p=0.3820: gain(iid=lam 0) =     +4.73   max gain =    +45.03 at lam2=3   [n(1-h(p)) = 40.6]
n=  1000 p=0.3900: gain(iid=lam 0) =     -7.73   max gain =    +39.09 at lam2=3   [n(1-h(p)) = 35.2]
n= 10000 p=0.3823: gain(iid=lam 0) =     +1.25   max gain =   +407.98 at lam2=3   [n(1-h(p)) = 403.5]
n= 10000 p=0.4200: gain(iid=lam 0) =   -594.69   max gain =   +124.34 at lam2=3   [n(1-h(p)) = 185.5]

Reading: the iid row is the CL barrier (negative gain above psi);
a moderate overlap tilt makes the union sweep the deleted middle
band -- gain ~ n(1-h(p)) = Theta(n).  The tilt detects the slice's
non-closure by PROBABILITY, not log-likelihood.
  [checkpoint: ../attempts/union-closed/data/003_partB.json]

