==============================================================================
E. Adversary hunt: 2-block product mixtures vs the single-lambda
   overlap-tilt recipe (asymptotic model)
==============================================================================
Model of the recipe's sweep over lam (per coordinate, n -> inf):
  lam = 0:      net_iid  = sum_{a,b} P_a P_b h(1-x_a x_b) - E h(p)
  lam > 0 fixed: net(rho) = sum_k P_k [h(1-z_rho(x_k,x_k))-h(p_k)]
               (blocks become assortative since n*lam -> inf)
Killer candidate = both <= 0 for all rho.  NOTE: intermediate
lam ~ gamma/n schedules are not modeled; a model-killer is a
necessary screen only.

